---
import Drift from "./Drift.astro";
import SectionHead from "./SectionHead.astro";
import Unused from "./Unused.astro";
---

<section class="bloat" id="bloat" aria-labelledby="bloat-title">
  <SectionHead no="02" name="Bloat" />
  <div class="card text-card">
    <h2 id="bloat-title">Most of what loads is never used.</h2>
    <p>
      This run loaded 26 MCP tools and called 2. The skill list offers 12 skills, and 3 were used in a month. Every
      unused tool and skill still takes its place in context on every call.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Unused />

  <div class="card text-card">
    <h2>A bloated context is one reason agents drift off task.</h2>
    <p>
      Here are the same run's tool calls, in order. It started well, then failed five times in a row, four of them the
      same blocked command. The history can't prove the load caused this. It does show what drift looks like, and
      Quench finds it.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Drift />
</section>
